The pyne amalgamation script sets an unused 'githash' variable via `git rev-parse HEAD`,
which fails when building from a release tarball (no .git directory). Because of `set -e`
the script then aborts BEFORE remove_unsupported.py stubs out the unsupported
Material::decay/Material::cram calls, leading to a compile error in pyne.cpp
("no member named 'transmuters' in namespace 'pyne'"). Comment the line out.

Author: Simon Pinches (ITER Organization)
--- DAGMC-3.2.4.orig/src/pyne/amalgamate_pyne.sh
+++ DAGMC-3.2.4/src/pyne/amalgamate_pyne.sh
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@
     src/source_sampling.*
 cp pyne.cpp pyne.h $2

-githash=`git rev-parse HEAD`
+#githash=`git rev-parse HEAD`  # unused, and fails (aborting the script via set -e) when building from a release tarball without .git
 cd $2
 python3 $1/remove_unsupported.py
 mv -fv pyne.cpp.new pyne.cpp
